// Pull request author: einlamye
// Change: new rule
// Title: Data Collection From Removable Media Via PowerShell
// Sigma ID: 22f05339-11ff-475c-9289-b349fd1660da
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: EinLamYe
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: collection, T1025
// Description: Detects PowerShell commands that enumerate removable/USB drives and recursively search them for
//   documents (e.g. .doc, .xls, .txt, .pdf). Adversaries scan removable media to locate and stage
//   sensitive documents for collection and exfiltration.
// False positives:
//   - Backup or data-management scripts that index documents on removable media
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/94153597065a5cb453168ae177f48c9d30e89edb/atomics/T1025/T1025.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/0963893c6b14acd541f16d39469e1acf1ac9a8f0/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_data_from_removable_media.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "DriveType -eq 'Removable'" or ProcessCommandLine contains "DriveType -eq \"Removable\"" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Get-Volume") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "Get-ChildItem" or ProcessCommandLine contains "gci " or ProcessCommandLine contains "ls ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains ".doc" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".xls" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".pdf" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".txt")
